%T A402341 29632604816,452466790336,6942916764720,106788367505456,
%U A402341 1648570691046736,25491847538274240,395320344293410544,6137695417757646851,95516115829966102480,1487718892458984362752
%N A402341 Central (largest) coefficient of (1 + x + x^2 + ... + x^15)^n.
%C A402341 a(n) is the size of a largest antichain in the product of n chains of 16 elements each (de Bruijn, Tengbergen, and Kruyswijk).
%C A402341 a(n) is odd if and only if n = (16^k - 1)/15 for some k >= 0, i.e., n = 0, 1, 17, 273, 4369, ... Proof: modulo 2, 1 + x + ... + x^15 == (1+x)^15, so a(n) == binomial(15*n, floor(15*n/2)) (mod 2). By Lucas's theorem, binomial(N, floor(N/2)) is odd iff N = 0 or N = 2^m - 1, and 15*n = 2^m - 1 holds iff 4 | m.
%C A402341 Conjecture: for even n, the 2-adic valuation of a(n) equals A000120(15*n/2). Verified for n <= 1500.
%D A402341 N. G. de Bruijn, Ca. van Ebbenhorst Tengbergen, and D. Kruyswijk, On the set of divisors of a number, Nieuw Archief voor Wiskunde (2) 23 (1951), 191-193.
%H A402341 Sajid Khan Hussain, <a href="/A402341/b402341.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..829</a>
%F A402341 a(n) ~ 16^n * sqrt(2/(85*Pi*n)).
%F A402341 a(n) = Sum_{j=0..floor(h/16)} (-1)^j * binomial(n,j) * binomial(n-1+h-16*j, n-1) with h = floor(15*n/2), n >= 1.
%F A402341 a(n) = Sum_{m>=0, m==n (mod 2)} c(n,m)*binomial(m, floor(m/2)), where c(n,m) is the coefficient of u^m in (u*(u^2-2)*(u^4-4*u^2+2)*(u^8-8*u^6+20*u^4-16*u^2+2))^n.
%e A402341 For n = 2, (1 + x + ... + x^15)^2 = 1 + 2*x + 3*x^2 + ... + 15*x^14 + 16*x^15 + 15*x^16 + ... + 2*x^29 + x^30, so a(2) = 16.
%e A402341 For n = 3, (1 + x + ... + x^15)^3 has degree 45 and its two middle coefficients, those of x^22 and x^23, are both 192, so a(3) = 192.
%t A402341 Table[Max[CoefficientList[Sum[x^j, {j, 0, 15}]^n, x]], {n, 0, 20}] (* _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 17 2026 *)
%o A402341 (PARI) a(n) = if(n==0, 1, polcoeff(((1-x^16)/(1-x) + O(x^(15*n\2+1)))^n, 15*n\2));
%o A402341 (PARI) a(n) = vecmax(Vec(sum(k=0,15,x^k)^n)); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Nov 17 2026
%o A402341 (Python)
%o A402341 from math import comb
%o A402341 def A402341(n):
%o A402341     if n == 0: return 1
%o A402341     h = 15*n//2
%o A402341     return sum((-1)**j*comb(n, j)*comb(n-1+h-16*j, n-1) for j in range(h//16+1))
